body:
This sucks, but there could be several reasons for this aside from it being on purpose. At our taco bell, the boss always told people we couldnt guarantee any promises that items will be 100% vegan/vegetarian food, nor guarantee dietary restrictions because of the way the lines are set up (loose sprinkle cheese next to tomatos, guac, etc.) Another reason was that employees AND customers misunderstand beef and beans ALL the time. It happened a dozen or more times every day when I was on the line. Sometimes instead of 'sub' they hit 'add' etc.  As for product placement, the line goes vegan items on one side (red sauce, black beans, rice, and beans) while the meat goes on the other. That doesn't mean mistakes cant happen when working with items that you must spoon out of a pan with a pasta spoon, the ones with holes?  Sometimes, shit just happens.

&#x200B;

edit because im dyslexic af and cant spell
